MMAANNUUAALL SSEECCUURRIITTYY AASSSSOOCCIIAATTIIOONNSS ((SSAAss))
     In this scenario, iippsseecc..ccoonnff is used to set up SAs manually.  The secu‐
     rity parameters for a flow are stored in the Security Association Data‐
     base (SADB).  An example of setting up an SA:

        # Set up an IPsec SA for flows between 192.168.3.14 and 192.168.3.12
        esp from 192.168.3.14 to 192.168.3.12 spi 0xdeadbeef:0xbeefdead \
                authkey file "auth14:auth12" enckey file "enc14:enc12"

     Parameters specify the peers, Security Parameter Index (SPI), crypto‐
     graphic transforms, and key material to be used.  The following rules en‐
     ter SAs in the SADB:

           eesspp       Enter an ESP SA.
           aahh        Enter an AH SA.
           iippccoommpp    Enter an IPCOMP SA.
           iippiipp      Enter an IPIP pseudo SA.
           ttccppmmdd55    Enter a TCP MD5 SA.

     The commands are as follows:

     _m_o_d_e  For ESP and AH the encapsulation mode can be specified.  Possible
           modes are _t_u_n_n_e_l and _t_r_a_n_s_p_o_r_t.  When left out, _t_u_n_n_e_l is chosen.
           For details on modes see ipsec(4).

     ffrroomm _s_r_c ttoo _d_s_t
           This SA is for a _f_l_o_w between the peers _s_r_c and _d_s_t.

     ssppii _n_u_m_b_e_r
           The SPI identifies a specific SA.  _n_u_m_b_e_r is a 32-bit value and
           needs to be unique.

     uuddppeennccaapp [ppoorrtt _d_p_o_r_t]
           For NAT-Traversal encapsulate the IPsec traffic in UDP.  The port
           number of the peer can be set to _d_p_o_r_t.

     aauutthh _a_l_g_o_r_i_t_h_m
           For ESP and AH an authentication algorithm can be specified.  Pos‐
           sible values are described above in _C_R_Y_P_T_O _T_R_A_N_S_F_O_R_M_S.

           If no algorithm is specified, ipsecctl(8) will choose _h_m_a_c_-_s_h_a_2_-_2_5_6
           by default.

     eenncc _a_l_g_o_r_i_t_h_m
           For ESP an encryption algorithm can be specified.  Possible values
           are described above in _C_R_Y_P_T_O _T_R_A_N_S_F_O_R_M_S.

           If no algorithm is specified, ipsecctl(8) will choose _a_e_s by de‐
           fault.

